All examples are buildable under supported environments and build
procedures.

On Windows, run the WINDOWS command from the WINEXAM\SETUP directory
to install the NMAKE makefiles and icons into each example directory.
Then build individual examples with:

    nmake -f makefile.msc

On Linux/macOS (with Wine), each example directory already contains a
GNU makefile.  Build with:

    make

The following utility commands are available from the WINEXAM\SETUP
directory:

WINDOWS
Install NMAKE makefiles and icons into all example directories.

CLEANALL
Delete all files produced by builds in all examples.

REALCLN
Delete all files produced by builds and all build configuration
files (return to an as-shipped state).

CLEAN
Delete all files produced by a build for a single example
(execute from the particular example's directory).
